here is what i found in the file : 



HTTP Request Details





Method: POST



URL Path: /agents/{agent_id}/runs/{run_id}/continue





agent_id (Path parameter, Required): The ID of your agent (e.g. postgres_agent).



run_id (Path parameter, Required): The unique ID of the paused run.



Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded or multipart/form-data



2. Required Fields

Field Name	Type	Form Location	Description

session_id	str	Form Data	Required. The session ID associated with the paused run.

tools	str (JSON)	Form Data	Required when resuming a run that has pending tool execution / HITL approvals.<br>Must be a JSON string encoding an array of tool execution objects



Expected JSON Structure for tools:



[

  {

    "tool_call_id": "call_xyz123",

    "tool_name": "run_admin_sql",

    "tool_args": { "sql": "ALTER TABLE ..." },

    "content": "Action approved by human",

    "confirmed": true

  }

]



and these are just optional fields : 



Field Name	Type	Default	Description

input	str	None	Optional text to append to the run as a new user message.

continue_from	str	"end"	Where to resume from: "end", "last_user", or a numeric message index string.

stream	bool	true	Return real-time streaming response using SSE (text/event-stream). Set false for JSON response.

background	bool	false	Run in background detached task (survives client disconnect, requires DB).

user_id	str	None	User identifier for tracking context.

fork	bool	false	Clone the run with a new run_id before resuming instead of modifying the existing run.

regenerate	bool	false	Regenerate the last response (automatically sets continue_from='last_user').

replace_original	bool	true	Only used with regenerate=true. Hides the original response in history.

additional_instructions	str	None	Only used with regenerate=true. Appends extra prompt guidance.







